            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-R7MhdKkunoFcz3xpBWml3Q6tgYg\">Looking at developed nations with high vehicle numbers, Luxembourg led the group with 548 vehicles per thousand inhabitants in 1990, slightly higher than New Zealand's 531, while the Bahamas recorded a considerably lower figure of 235. By 2000, Luxembourg's number had risen to 728, and New Zealand saw a modest increase to 557 vehicles. In contrast, the Bahamas experienced a decline to 187 vehicles per thousand people.</div>\n</div>",
